$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Asymmetric Aldol Reactions Catalyzed by FeII
Salt: Mixture of TPS-he-pybox (3c) (47 mg, 0.06 mmol, 12 mol%) and
iron(II) chloride (6.5 mg, 0.05 mmol, 10 mol%) in deoxygenated EtOH/H2O
(9/1) 1.5 mL was stirred at 0 °C under Ar until all the solid was
observed to dissolve (15-20 min.). To the resulting deep-red solution
silyl enol ether 5 (230 μL, 1.0 mmol, 2 equivalents) and appropriate
aldehyde (0.5 mmol) were added and resulting solution was stirred at 0 °C
for 5 h under Ar. The reaction was diluted with MTBE and washed with
water and brine. Organic phase was dried, evaporated to dryness and the
residue was purified by silica gel chromatography (typically,
AcOEt/hexane, 1:4). (2S,3S)-3-Hydroxy-2-methyl-1,3-diphenyl-propan-1-one
(7a). 1H NMR (200 MHz) δ (syn): 1.19 (d, 3H, J 7.2 Hz), 3.67 (d, 1H, OH,
J 1.7 Hz), 4.11 (dq, 1H, J 3.0, 7.3 Hz), 5.23 (brs, 1H), 7.20 - 7.65 (m,
8H), 7.85-8.20 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (50 MHz) δ: 11.1, 47.1, 73.0, 125.9,
127.3, 128.2, 128.4, 128.7, 133.5, 135.6, 141.7, 205.8. [α]D +3.5 (c 0.1
in CHCl3, 85% ee), lit.[4] for syn-(2S,3S)-5a: [α]D +11.7 (c 1.03 in
CHCl3, 95% ee); HPLC (Daicel Chiralpak AD-H, hexane/i-PrOH = 9/1, flow
rate = 1 mL/min; syn isomer: t1 = 9.9 min, t2 = 12.2 min (major), anti
isomer: t1 = 14.6 min, t2 = 16.0 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
