$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure C: Aldol reactions between aldehydes
and 1-phenyl-l-(trimethylsilyoxy)ethvlene (7): To aldehyde (3.0 mmol) in
a dry flask under N2 were added THF (anhydrous, 15 mL) and
l-phenyl-l-(trimethylsilyoxy)ethylene (0.75 mL, 3.60 mmol based on 98%
purity). The solution was cooled to -30 °C and carbene 5 (5 mg, 0.014
mmol) was added in one portion. The mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 65 h.
HC1 aq solution (1 N, 3 mL) was added and the solution was stirred at 23
°C for 1 h. Saturated NaHCO3 aq solution (3 mL) and water (3 mL) were
added. Dichloromethane (60 mL) was added and the aqueous layer was
extracted with dichloromethane (30 mL). Organic layers were combined and
solvents were removed under vacuum to give the crude residue, which was
purified by silica gel flash chromatography (ethyl acetate/hexanes) to
give product in yield indicated below. Compound 8h was prepared by using
Procedure C and isolated by silica gel flash chromatography (10%
EtOAc/hexanes) in 84% yield. 1H NMR (CDC13, 400 MHz) δ 8.26-8.22 (m, 2H),
7.96-7.94 (m, 2H), 7.64-7.60 (m, 3H), 7.51-7.47 (m, 2H), 5.47-5.45 (m,
1H), 3.87 (d, J = 2.9 Hz, 1H), 3.45-3.31 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (CDC13, 100
MHz) δ 199.5, 150.2, 147.4, 136.1, 134.1, 128.9, 128.2, 126.6, 123.8,
69.2, 47.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Heterocyclic Carbene-Catalyzed Mukaiyama Aldol Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
