$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure A: Aldol reactions between aldehydes
and methyl trimethylsilyl dimethylketene acetal (2): To aldehyde (3.0
mmol) in a dry flask under N2 were added THF (anhydrous, 15 rnL), methyl
trimethylsilyl dimethylketene acetal (0.66 g, 3.60 mmol based on 95%
purity) and carbene 5 (5 mg, 0.014 mmol). The mixture was stirred at 23
°C for 3 h. HC1 solution (1 N, 3 mL) was added and the solution was
stirred at 23 °C for 1 h. Saturated NaHCO3 aq solution (3 mL) and water
(3 mL) were added. Dichloromethane (50 mL) was added and the aqueous
layer was extracted with dichloromethane (50 mL). Organic layers were
combined and solvents were removed under vacuum to give the crude
residue, which was purified by silica gel flash chromatography (ethyl
acetate/hexanes) to give pure product Compound 6f was prepared by using
Procedure A and isolated by silica gel flash chromatography (5-35%
EtOAc/hexanes) in 81% yield. 1H NMR (CDC13, 400 MHz) δ 7.29 (d, J = 8.4
Hz, 2H), 7.22 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 4.85 (d, J = 3.5 Hz, 1H), 3.70 (s,
3H), 3.37 (d, J = 4.1 Hz, 1H), 1.11 (s, 3H), 1.08 (s, 3H). 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 178.1, 138.5, 133.5, 129.0, 127.9, 77.9, 52.2, 47.6,
22.8, 19.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Heterocyclic Carbene-Catalyzed Mukaiyama Aldol Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
