$DATUM (S, E)-Diethyl 7-hydroxy-4,4-dimethyl-5-oxooct-2-enedioate (10) To a
solution of (S)-6,6'-dibromobinaphthol (34.6 mg, 78.0 μmol, 0.20 equiv)
in Et2O (1.60 mL) was added 4 Å MS (98.0 mg) and Ti(Oz-Pr)4 (23.0 μL,
78.0 μmol, 0.20 equiv). The red-brownish suspension was stirred for 1 h
at r.t. and was then cooled to 0 °C. Freshly distilled ethyl glyoxalate
(4) (57 μL, 485 μmol, 86% in toluene, 1.25 equiv) and silyl enol ether 3
(102 mg, 398 μmol, 1.00 equiv), dissolved in Et2O (0.40 mL), were
consecutively added via syringe. The reaction mixture was vigorously
stirred overnight, quenched with sat. aq NH4Cl and warmed to r.t. It was
diluted with a mixture of Et2O-H2O (3:1, 20 mL) and filtered over a plug
of cotton. The layers were separated and the aqueous layer was extracted
with Et2O (3x). The combined organic layer was washed with 1 M aq HCl
(2x), sat. aq NaHCO3 (1x), brine (1 x) and dried over MgSO4. Filtration
of solids and evaporation of solvents gave a crude oil which was purified
by column chromatography (PE-EtOAc = 80:20) to obtain aldol 10 as an oil;
ee &gt;98% [HPLC: n-heptane-i-PrOH (98:2), flow = 0.5 mL/min]: tR (6a) =
54.9 minutes. Colorless oil, (95.6 mg, 334 μmol, 84%). [a]D20 +3.6 (c
1.09, CHCl3); Rf= 0.40 (PE-EtOAc = 70:60). 1HNMR (600 MHz, CDCl3):δ= 1.28
(t,3J = 7.3 Hz, 3 H, 10-H or 2'-H), 1.30 (t,3J = 7.4 Hz, 3 H, 10-H or
2'-H), 1.29 (s, 3 H, 4-CH3a), 1.30 (s, 3 H, 4-CH3b), 2.95 (dd, 2J6a,6b =
17.7 Hz,3J6a,7 = 5.7 Hz, 1 H, 6-Ha), 2.99 (dd,2J6a,6b = 17.7 Hz, 3J6b,7
=4.0 Hz, 1 H, 6-Hb), 3.11 (d, 3J7-OH,7 = 5.4 Hz, 1 H, 7-OH), 4.21 (q, 3J=
7.4 Hz, 2 H, 9-H or 1'-H), 4.24 (q, 3J= 7.3 Hz, 2 H, 9-H or 1'-H), 4.45
(ddd, 3J76, a = 5.5 Hz, 3J7,7-OH= 5.4 Hz, 3J76, b = 4.1 Hz, 1 H, 7-H),
5.90 (d, 3J2,3 = 15.9 Hz, 1 H, 2-H), 7.00 (d,3J3,2 = 15.9 Hz, 1 H, 3-H)
ppm. 13CNMR (151 MHz, CDCl3):δ= 14.1, 14.2 (C-10 und C-2'), 23.3
(4-CH3a),23.3 (CH3b), 41.8 (C-6), 50.5 (C-4), 60.6, 61.9 (C-9 and C-1'),
66.9 (C-7), 121.4 (C-2), 150.4 (C-3), 166.1 (C-1), 173.7 (C-8), 208.6
(C-5) ppm. IR (film): ν = 3493, 2981, 2937, 1709,1647,1467,1389,
1367,1298, 1268, 1181, 1096,1061,1032, 988, 865, 723 cm-1. Anal. Calcd
for: C, 58.73; H, 7.74. Found: C, 58.46; H, 7.73.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, optimization study, key step, Mukaiyama aldol reaction,
optimized on catalyst, ligand, solvent and temperature, molecular sieves
used in stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An enantioselective Mukaiyama aldol reaction as the key step towards the
tetrahydropyran core of psymberin via a γ-butyrolactone intermediate
