$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3.2. Diastereoselective Mukaiyama aldol
reaction of cyclohexanones with acyclic ketene acetals Ethyl
(1-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)cyclohexyl)acetate (4a) 3.3. Mukaiyama
aldol reaction of acyclic ketones with acyclic ketene acetals Ethyl
3-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-2,2-dimethyl-3-pentyloctanoate (5a)
According to the synthetic procedure for 4a, this compound was obtained
in 83% yield (331.4 mg, 0.83 mmol) by the reaction of undecan-6-one 2g
(205 μL, 1.0 mmol) with
tert-butyl(1-ethoxy-2-methylpropenyloxy)-dimethylsilane (346.4 mg, 1.5
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2.0 mL) in the presence of Tf2CHCH2CHTf2 1 (5.7 mg, 10
μmol) for 2.5 h at -124 °C, then for 1 h at 0 °C. Colorless oil;. IR
(neat) ν 2957, 2928, 2857, 1724, 1255, 1122, 1064, 834, 770 cm-1; 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.11 (6H, s), 0.87 (9H, s), 0.89 (6H, s), 1.17-1.36
(12H, m), 1.22 (6H, s), 1.25 (3H, t, J = 7.1 Hz), 1.62-1.70 (2H, m),
1.70-1.79 (2H, m), 4.06 (2H, q, J = 7.1 Hz); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ
