$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for 1,2-chelation control
Mukaiyama aldol reactions To a solution of 0.3 mmol of the aldehyde 5 in
3.0 mL of dichloromethane was added 1.2 equiv. of SnCl4 at –78 °C After
the reaction stirred for 5 min, a pre-cooled dichloromethane solution
containing 1.2 equiv. of the (Z)-enol silane was added slowly. After the
mixture stirred at –78 °C for 1 h, the solution was allowed to warm to
-50 ° and the stirring was continued until the solution became clear. The
reaction was quenched with saturated NaHCO2 and resulting mixture was
extracted with diethyl ether. The combined organic extracts was washed
with water, brine and dried over MgSO4. The residue, after concentration
in vacuo, was purified by flash chromatography.
(2S,3S,4R,6R,7S,8S)-3-Hydroxy-7-[(1,1-dimethylethyl)dimethylsilyloxy]-1,9-bis[(1,1-dimethylethyl)
diphenylsilyloxy]-4,6-dimethyl-2,8-bis(phenylmethoxy)nonan-5-one (30). 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.78 (m, 4H), 7.72 (t, J = 6.5 Hz, 4H), 7.35-7.49
(m, 18H), 7.28 (m, 4H), 4.77 (d, J = 11.5 Hz, 1H), 4.72 (ABq, J = 9.0 Hz,
2H), 4.41 (d, J = 11.5 Hz, 1H), 4.22 (dd, J = 9.5, 3.5 Hz, 1H), 3.94 (m,
5H), 3.67 (quintet, J = 3.5 Hz, 1H), 3.49 (t, J = 5.0 Hz, 1H), 2.82
(quintet, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H), 2.68 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 1H), 1.09 (s, 9H), 1.08
(s, 9H), 1.08 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 0.83 (s, 9H), 0.74 (d, J = 7.0 Hz,
3H), 0.03 (s, 3H), –0.05 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 214.97,
138.79, 138.13, 135.55, 135.53, 135.49, 133.24, 133.21, 133.02, 129.65,
129.52, 129.50, 128.18, 128.10, 127.99, 127.63, 127.60, 127.56, 127.35,
126.71, 82.73, 77.32, 76.63, 72.52, 72.18, 71.51, 63.56, 49.25, 47.84,
26.75, 26.58, 25.82, 18.99, 17.91, 13.28, 12.14, -4.44, -5.35. MS
(MALDI-TOF) m/z calcd for C63H84O7Si3 (M+Na)+ 1059.54, Found 1059.42.
