$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7. A general procedure for 4b·L2-catalyzed Mukaiyama aldol reaction with
ketones: Freshly distilled THF (5 mL) was injected at room temperature
under nitrogen into pyrex Schrenk tube containing sodium phenoxide (5b)
(2.9 mg, 0.025 mmol) and 1,2-bis(diphenylphosphoryl)benzene (L) (23.9 mg,
0.050 mmol). The mixture was stirred for 10 min at that temperature, and
then this colorless solution was cooled to –78 °C and stirred for 5 min
at that temperature. methyl
2,2-dimethyl-4-oxo-3,4-diphenyl-3-(trimethylsilyloxy)butanoate (3p):8 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.09 (s, 9H), 1.18 (s, 3H), 1.19 (s, 3H), 3.71 (s,
3H), 4.34 (m, 2H), 7.15-7.70 (m, 10H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.6,
22.2, 24.8, 49.8, 51.7, 89.2, 127.5, 127.5, 127.6, 127.7, 131.2, 132.3,
135.5, 140.7, 177.4, 199.0. IR(film) 2953, 1732, 1687, 1272, 1250, 1147,
1130, 1081 cm-1. HRMS(FAB+) calcd for C22H28NaO4Si [M+Na]+ 407.1655,
found 407.1660.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mukaiyama aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Sodium Phenoxide-Phosphine Oxides as Extremely Active Lewis Base
Catalysts for the Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction with Ketones
