$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical procedure (Table 2, entry 1) : To a suspension of 180 mg of
Bi(OTf)3·4H2O (246 μmol, 1 mol %) in 20 mL of dichloromethane was added
at -70 °C, 3.18 g (27 mmol) of benzaldehyde dimethylacetal in
dichloromethane (3 mL). Then, 4.74 g (24.6 mmol) of α
-trimethylsilyloxystyrene in dichloromethane (3 mL) was added and the
reaction mixture was stirred for 15 min. After this time, water (15 mL)
was added and the products were extracted twice with 2 x 20 mL of
dichloromethane. The combined organic phases were dried (MgSO4) and
concentrated. The crude product was purified by flash chromatography on
silica gel to give product. Compound 4a. Yield 4.84 g 82%. IR (neat) 1682
cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 3.0 (dd, 1H, J = 4.6 and 16.4 Hz, CH2CO), 3.2 (s,
3H, OMe), 3.6 (dd, 1H, J = 8.2 and 16.4 Hz, CH2CO), 4.9 (dd, 1H, J = 4.6
and 8.2 Hz, CHO), 7.3-7.5 (m, 8H, Ph), 7.8-8.0 (m, 2H, Ph).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bismuth(III) triflate. A water-stable equivalent of trimethylsilyl
triflate for the catalysis of Mukaiyama aldol reactions
