$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the aldol reaction To a
stirred solution of the aldehyde 1c (130 mg, 236 μmol) in freshly
distilled CH2Cl2 (5 mL) cooled to -60 °C was added the BF3.OEt2 (90 μL,
710 μmol) with a syringe. After 5 min 7 (102 μL, 472 μmol) was added and
the mixture stirred at -60 °C for 18h. The reaction was quenched with
saturated NaHCO3 (5 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3x10 mL). The combined
organic phases were dried (MgSO4), filtered and evaporated to give a
colorless oil. The diastereomeric ratio was determined by 1H NMR on the
crude reaction mixture. Flash chromatography of the residue
(pentane:EtOAc 20:1) yielded 3b (141 mg, 92%) as a colorless oil.
N-Benzyl-N-{(1R*,2R*)-1-[(S*)-1-(tert-butyl-dimethyl-silanyloxy)-3-phenyl-propyl]-2-hydroxy-5,5-dimethyl-4-oxo-hexyl}-4-methyl-benzenesulfonamide
(4c) 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.75 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.51 (d, J = 6.8
Hz, 2H), 7.37-7.18 (m, 10H), 4.81 (d, J = 15.2 Hz, 1H), 4.40 (d, J = 15.2
Hz, 1H), 4.24 (m, 1H,), 4.07 (m, 1H), 3.91 (m, 1H), 3.64 (d, J = 2.3 Hz,
1H), 2.88 (dt, J = 13.0, 4.6 Hz, 1H), 2.69 (m, 1H), 2.61 (dt, J = 13.0,
4.6 Hz, 1H), 2.45 (s, 3H), 2.21 (d, 18 Hz, 1H), 2.0 (m, 1H), 1.63 (m,
1H), 1.03 (s, 9H), 0.92 (s, 9H), 0.02 (s, 3H), -0.02 (s, 3H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 215.6, 143.5, 142.6, 138.0, 137.7, 129.8, 129.0,
128.6, 128.5, 128.3, 127.7, 127.3, 125.6, 72.4, 68.9, 44.0, 41.6, 35.8,
28.8, 26.0, 21.4, 18.1, -4.3, -4.4; IR (neat) 2960, 1690, 1160 cm-1; HRMS
(FAB+) calcd for C37H54NO5SSi (M+H): 652.3492, found: 652.3484.
