$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Asymmetric Aldol
Reactions Catalyzed by ZnII Salt: Mixture of TPS-he-pybox (3c) (23 mg,
0.03 mmol, 12 mol%) and zinc(II) trifluoromethanesulfonate (9 mg, 0.025
mmol, 10 mol%) in EtOH/H2O (9/1) 1.0 mL was stirred at -20 °C (15-20
min.). To the resulting homogeneous solution silyl enol ether 5 (115 μL,
0.5 mmol, 2 equivalents) and appropriate aldehyde (0.25 mmol) were added
and resulting homogeneous solution was left in refrigerator at -20 °C
overnight without stirring. The reaction mixture was poured onto silica
gel column and eluted by AcOEt/hexane (1:4) to yield desired aldols.
3-(4-Chlorophenyl)-3-hydroxy-2-methyl-1-phenyl- propan-1-one (7f). 1H NMR
(200 MHz) δ (syn): 1.17 (d, 3H, J 7.2 Hz), 3.64 (dq, 1H, J 3.2, 7.3 Hz),
3.82 (d, 1H, J 1.9 Hz), 5.20 (t, 1H, J 3.0 Hz), 7.25-7.65 (m, 8H),
7.88-8.10 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (50 MHz) δ: 11.1, 46.8, 72.4, 127.4, 127.9,
128.6, 128.8, 132.9, 133.6, 135.4, 140.3, 205.4. HPLC (Daicel Chiralpak
AD-H, hexane/i-PrOH = 9/1, flow rate = 1 mL/min; syn isomer: t1 = 11.1
min, t2 = 12.5 min (major), anti isomer: t1 = 15.7 min (major), t2 = 20.6
min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mukaiyama-Aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Iron(II) and Zinc(II) Complexes with Designed pybox Ligand for Asymmetric
Aqueous Mukaiyama-Aldol Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Jankowska, Joanna; Paradowska, Joanna; Rakiel, Bartosz; Mlynarski, Jacek
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2007), 72(6), 2228-2231

