$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Aldehyde 12: To a solution of N-Ts-L-tryptophan (892 mg, 2.5 mmol, 0.2
eq.) in methylene chloride (25 ml) was added boron dichloride 34 (490 μL,
735 mg 2.5 mmol, 0.2 eq) at room temperature and stirred for 60 min. The
solvent was removed in vacuo and the resulting solid dried under reduced
pressure for 30 min. The so obtained oxazaborolidinone was dissolved in
propionitrile (20 mL). Trimethylborate (696 μL, 457 mg, 6.3 mmol, 0.5 eq)
was added at room temperature and the reaction mixture was cooled to -78
°C. A solution of aldehyde 7 (3.50 g, 12.5 mmol, 1.0 eq) in propionitrile
(10 mL) was slowly added and afterwards a solution of enolether 11 (2.56
mL, 2.15 g, 13.8 mmol, 1.1 eq) in propionitrile (10 mL) was added over 10
min. After 12 h the reaction was quenched by the addition of a mixture of
tetrahydrofurane (50 mL), water (10 mL), and hydrochloric acid (2 M, 2
mL). It was warmed to room temperature and stirred for 30 min. Methyl
tert-butyl ether (50 mL) and saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution (50 mL)
was added and the aqueous layer was extracted with methyl tert-butyl
ether (3x10 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with brine (50
mL), dried over MgSO4, filtered, and the solvent removed in vacuo. It was
dried over MgSO4, filtered and the solvent was removed in vacuo.
determined by chiral GC) (25% EtOAc/PE) and was obtained by column
chromatography. Aldehyde 10 as a yellow oil, yield 2.85 g, 10.2 mmol,
82%, 91% ee. [α]20D = +3.8 (c = 0.4, CHCl3); Rf = 0.35 (30% EtOAc/PE); 1H
NMR (400 MHz, C6D6) δ = 9.21 (s, 1H), 5.97 - 5.95 (m, 1H), 5.95 - 5.89
(m, 1H), 3.57 - 3.50 (m, 1H), 2.06 - 1.86 (m, 2H), 1.60 - 1.51 (m, 6H)
ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, C6D6) δ 193.8, 149.4, 148.2, 141.1, 78.9, 75.0,
34.4, 19.9, 9.4 ppm; APCI-HRMS: C9H13O2ICl [M+Cl]- calculated: 314.9649,
found: 314.9655.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 91% e.e., vinylogous Mukaiyama aldol reaction, key step
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Angiolam A
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gieseler, Marc Timo; Kalesse, Markus
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(2), 548-551

