$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3.2. Diastereoselective Mukaiyama aldol
reaction of cyclohexanones with acyclic ketene acetals Ethyl
(1-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)cyclohexyl)acetate (4a) Ethyl
3-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-2,2-dimethyl-3,3-diphenylpropanoate (5c)
According to the synthetic procedure for 4a, this compound was obtained
in 82% yield (340.0 mg, 0.82 mmol) by the reaction of benzophenone 2i
(182.2 mg, 1.0 mmol) with
tert-butyl(1-ethoxy-2-methylpropenyloxy)-dimethylsilane (345.0 mg, 1.5
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2.0 mL) in the presence of Tf2CHCH2CHTf2 1 (5.7 mg, 10
μmol) for 2.5 h at -124 °C. Colorless oil;. IR (neat) ν 3059, 2955, 2856,
1735, 1254, 1129, 1094, 1072, 834, 706 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
-10.38 (6H, s), 0.99 (9H, s), 1.17 (3H, t, J = 7.1 Hz), 1.36 (6H, s),
4.06 (2H, q, J = 7.1 Hz), 7.20-7.26 (6H, m), 7.36-7.40 (4H, m); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ -13.0, 14.0, 19.7, 24.5, 26.7, 51.2, 60.4, 86.1,
126.6, 127.1, 130.3, 145.3, 176.9; MS (ESI-TOF) m/z 435 [M+Na]+; HRMS
calcd for C25H36NaO3Si [M+Na]+, 435.2331; found, 435.2314.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
