$DATUM (5S,7R)-Methyl5-Hydroxy-7-((4-methoxybenzyl)oxy)-3-oxooctanoate (4) Under
an N2 atmosphere, 0.43mL TiCl4 (3.89mmol) was added to a solution of
1.3mL Ti(OiPr)4 (4.24mmol) in 40mL PhCH3 in a dropwise fashion at 0°C.
The solution was stirred at 0°C for 10min, and then cooled to -78°C to
give a milky white slurry. This slurry was treated with a solution of the
aldehyde 6 (1.46g, 7mmol) in PhCH3 (20.7mL) via a cannula. The resulting
solution was stirred at -78°C for another 10min before being treated with
a solution of the bis-(trimethylsilyl)dienol ether 5 (3.28g, 12.6mmol) in
PhCH3 (10mL).The reaction mixture was stirred at -78°C for 2h before
being quenched with saturated NH4Cl solution. The mixture was filtered
through a plug of celite and extracted with DCM (3x80mL). The combined
organic layer was washed with brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4,
filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by silica-gel column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc=10:1) to
provide a compound 4 Yellow oil, yield 1.86g, 82%. [α]25 D = -30:2
(c=0.54, CH2Cl2); 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.18 (d, J = 8.5Hz, 2H), 6.79
(d, J = 8.5Hz, 2H), 4.47 (d, J = 11.0Hz, 1H), 4.27 (d, J = 11.0 Hz, 2H),
4.22-4.10 (m, 1H), 3.78-3.73 (m, 1H), 3.71 (s, 3H), 3.64 (s, 3H), 3.40
(s, 2H), 3.26 (d, J = 3.6Hz, 1H), 2.60-2.53 (m, 2H), 1.64-1.46 (m, 2H),
1.15 (d, J = 6.0Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3): δ 202.8, 167.3, 159.0,
130.3, 129.2, 113.7, 71.6, 70.1, 64.6, 55.1, 52.2, 49.8, 49.5, 42.6,
19.2. HRMS (ESI): m/z calcd. for C17H24O6Na [M+Na]+ 347.1465; found
347.1467.
