$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (13) General Procedure for the Vinylogous
Asymmetric Mukaiyama-Type Aldol Reaction. A flame-dried Schlenk flask
under Ar atmosphere was charged with Cu(OTf)2 (18.1 mg, 0.05 mmol) and
aminosulfoximine 1 (0.05 mmol). Then, dry Et2O (2 mL) was added, and the
resulting deep green solution was stirred for 30 min at room temperature.
Subsequently, pyruvate ester 2 (0.5 mmol), vinyl ketene acetal 5 (0.55
mmol), and 2,2,2- trifluoroethanol (0.6 mmol, 44 μL) were added. After
stirring for the indicated period of time, trifluoroacetic acid (0.2 mL)
was added, and the solution was stirred for 30 min. The reaction mixture
was then diluted with Et2O, and a saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3
was added slowly. The aqueous layer was extracted three times with Et2O,
and the combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4. The solvent was
removed, and the product was purified by flash chromatography.
(R)-E-5-Hydroxy-5-methyl-hex-2-enedioc acid 1-tert-butyl ester 6-ethyl
ester (6cA): The product was prepared according to the general procedure
(see footnote 13 in text) using ethyl pyruvate (2c, 55 μL, 0.5 mmol) and
silyl vinyl ketene acetal 5A (141 mg, 0.55 mmol). It was obtained as
colorless oil in 81% yield (104 mg, 0.40 mmol) after flash chromatography
(pentane/EtOAc: 9/1). [α]D20 = −3.3 (c = 1.2, CHCl3); 1H-NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 1.30 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H, CH3), 1.44 (s, 3H, CH3), 1.47 (s,
9H, tBu), 2.49-2.63 (m, 2H, CH2), 2.92 (br s, 1H, OH), 4.21-4.30 (m, 2H,
CH2), 5.80 (d, J = 15.4 Hz, 1H, CH), 6.73-6.81 (m, 1H, CH) ppm; 13 C- NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 14.2, 25.8, 28.1, 42.5, 62.1, 73.8, 80.2, 126.6,
140.8, 165.1, 175.8 ppm; MS (70 eV, EI): m/z (%) = 259 (1) [M+H+], 129
(38), 111 (51), 86 (77), 57 (100); IR (film): ν = 3511, 2935, 1717, 1296,
1161 cm-1 ; elemental analysis (%) calcd for C13H22O5 (258.31): C 60.45,
H 8.58; found: C 60.41, H 8.27. The enantiomer ratio was determined by
HPLC analysis using a Chiralcel AD column (flow rate 0.4 mL/min,
heptane/iPrOH: 98/2, λ = 230 nm, 25 °C); tr = 41.3 min [major], tr = 51.0
min [minor]; 91% ee (97% ee when the reaction is performed at -78 °C).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, reaction at low temp. gave higher stereoselectivity but
lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Sulfoximines as Ligands in Copper-Catalyzed Asymmetric Vinylogous
Mukaiyama-Type Aldol Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Remy, Pauline; Langner, Martin; Bolm, Carsten
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(6), 1209-1211

