$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure 1: Preparation of δ
-Benzyloxy α-Seleno (or α-Bromo) Esters 9-18 via Mukaiyama Reaction
(Reverse Addition Mode). To a solution of aldehyde 4 or 5 (1 equiv) in
dry CH2Cl2 (0.05M with MgBr2.OEt2 and 0.1M with other Lewis acids) was
added the appropriate enoxysilane (see Table 1 for the appropriate number
of equivalents) under nitrogen atmosphere at the appropriate temperature
(see Table 1). The solution was stirred for 10 min at the same
temperature before the slow addition of the appropriate Lewis acid (see
Table 1 for the number of equivalents). The resulting solution was
stirred until the aldehyde was completely consumed; at least 1h when
MgBr2.OEt2 was employed with silylketene acetal 6; at least 4h when
MgBr2.OEt2 was employed with silylketene acetal 7 and as determined by
TLC with other Lewis acids. When the reaction was complete, a saturated
aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (with MgBr2·OEt2, BF3·OEt2 or Et2BOTf) or
NH4Cl (with Me2AlCl or TiCl4) was poured into the reaction mixture. After
the aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (3 X), the organic layers were
combined, successively washed with brine, dried (MgSO4), filtered and
concentrated.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, the yield and stereoselectivity depend on the reaction
conditions and on the Lewis acid used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Tertiary and Quaternary Stereogenic Centers: A
Diastereoselective Tandem Reaction Sequence Combining Mukaiyama and Free
Radical-Based Allylation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cardinal-David, Benoit; Guerin, Brigitte; Guindon, Yvan
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2005), 70(3), 776-784

