$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (1'R,2S,4''R,5''R,5'''R)-2-[Hydroxy-(2,2,2',2'-tetramethyl-[4,4']bis[[1,3]dioxolanyl]-5-yl)methyl]-5-oxo-2,5-dihydropyrrole-1-carboxylic
Acid tert-Butyl Ester (20). To a solution of
2,3:4,5-di-O-isopropylidene-D-arabinose (19) (3.0 g, 13.0 mmol) in
anhydrous Et2O (80 mL),
N-(tert-butoxycarbonyl)-2-[(tert-butyldimethyl)siloxy]pyrrole (12) (4.65
g, 15.6 mmol) and SnCl4 (1M in CH2Cl2, 15.63 mL, 15.6 mmol) were added
under argon at -80 °C. After being stirred at this temperature for 3 h,
the reaction mixture was quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution
and, after ambient temperature was reached, the resulting mixture was
extracted with Et2O. After drying (MgSO4), the combined extracts were
evaporated under reduced pressure and the crude product was purified by
silica gel flash chromatography (1:1 hexanes/EtOAc). Pure lactam 20 (4.36
g, 81%) was obtained as a white solid
(1'R,2S,4''R,5''R,5'''R)-2-[Hydroxy-(2,2,2',2'-tetramethyl-[4,4']bis[[1,3]dioxolanyl]-5-yl)methyl]-5-oxo-2,5-dihydropyrrole-1-carboxylic
Acid tert-Butyl Ester (20), (4.36 g, 81%) yield m.p. 150-152 °C; [α]20D
-144.5 (c 1.3, CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.37 (dd, J = 6.0, 2.0
Hz, 1H), 6.17 (dd, J = 6.4, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 4.81 (dt, J = 4.0, 2.0 Hz, 1H),
4.30 (ddd, J = 10.8, 4.0, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 4.26 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H), 4.18 (m,
1H), 4.00 (m, 2H), 3.73 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 3.55 (dd, J = 9.2, 7.2 Hz,
1H), 1.55 (s, 9H), 1.47 (s, 3H), 1.37 (s, 3H), 1.30 (s, 3H), 1.26 (s,
3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 168.9, 149.2, 146.9, 127.8, 109.8, 109.7,
82.1, 81.1, 79.5, 75.7, 70.6, 67.0, 65.0, 27.7 (3C), 26.2, 26.1, 25.8,
24.6. Anal. Calcd for C20H31NO8: C, 58.10; H, 7.56; N, 3.39. Found: C,
57.97; H, 7.45; N, 3.45.
