$DATUM (1'S,4''R,5R,5''S)-5-[(5-Benzyloxymethyl-2,2-dimethyl-[1,3]dioxolan-4-yl)hydroxymethyl]-5H-furan-2-one
(7). Protected L-threose 5 (4.94 g, 19.7 mmol) and
2-[(tert-butyldimethylsilyl)oxy]furan (6) (5.07 g, 25. 6 mmol) were
dissolved in CH2Cl2 (100 mL) under argon, and the mixture was cooled to
-80 °C. BF3 etherate (2.42 mL, 19.7 mmol) was added and the resulting
mixture was stirred for 6 h. A saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution was
added at -80 °C and, after ambient temperature was reached, the resulting
mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2. After drying (MgSO4), the solution was
evaporated under reduced pressure to give a residue which was subjected
to silica gel flash chromatography (1:1 hexanes/EtOAc). Pure lactone 7
(5.26 g, 80%) was obtained as an oil:
(1'S,4''R,5R,5''S)-5-[(5-Benzyloxymethyl-2,2-dimethyl-[1,3]dioxolan-4-yl)hydroxymethyl]-5H-furan-2-one
(7), 5.26 g, 80% yield [α]20D +12.0 (c 1.1, CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.48 (dd, J = 6.0, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.31 (m, 5H), 6.17 (dd, J = 6.0,
2.0 Hz, 1H), 5.25 (dt, J = 2.4, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 4.60 (1/2 ABq, J = 12.4 Hz,
1H), 4.54 (1/2 ABq, J = 12.4 Hz, 1H), 4.06 (td, J = 7.6, 4.8 Hz, 1H),
3.97 (dd, J = 8.4, 7.2 Hz, 1H), 3.76 (dd, J = 9.2, 4.8 Hz, 1H), 3.72 (dt,
J = 8.8, 2.8 Hz, 1H), 3.61 (d, J = 3.8 Hz, 1H), 3.53 (dd, J = 9.2, 8.0
Hz, 1H), 1.39 (s, 3H), 1.38 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.0,
153.9, 136.9, 128.2 (2C), 127.6 (3C), 121.9, 109.6, 83.5, 79.0, 78.1,
73.4, 72.2, 70.4, 26.6 (2C). Anal. Calcd for C18H22O6: C, 64.66; H, 6.63.
Found: C, 64.51; H, 6.73.
