$DATUM 75-05-8
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A typical procedure for Mannich-type reaction.
To a suspension of PMI Sc(OTf)3 (136 mg, 0.025 mmol, 10 mol%) in CH3CN
(3.0 mL) were added a solution of N-benzylideneaniline (45 mg, 0.25 mmol)
in CH3CN (1.0 mL) and a solution of ketene silyl acetal derived from
methyl isobutyrate (65 mg, 0.37 mmol) in CH3CN (1.0 mL) at 0 °C under Ar.
The mixture was stirred for 10 min at the same temperature and stirred
for 3 h at room temperature. After filtration and washing (CH2Cl2,
hexane), the filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure. The
divided crude compounds (see: ICP analysis section) were purified by PTLC
to give methyl 2,2-dimethyl-3-phenyl-3-(N-phenylamino)propionate (35 mg,
49% (corrected yield; 98%)). PMI Sc(OTf)3 was recovered quantitatively (>
97%), and reused, the 2nd run; 99%, 3rd run; 97%. In the 2nd and 3rd use,
all recovered crude compounds after the reaction were treated to
determine the yield of the desired compound. Methyl
3-(N’-benzoylhydrazino)-2,2-dimethyl-5-phenylpentanoate (entry 5):8 Pale
yellow oil; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ = 1.18 (s, 3H), 1.25 (s, 3H), 1.62–1.82 (m,
2H), 2.72–2.82 (m, 1H), 2.98–3.08 (m, 1H), 3.18 (dd, J = 9.6 and 2.4 Hz,
1H), 3.57 (s, 3H), 4.80 (br s, 1H), 7.10–7.27 (m, 5H), 7.35–7.54 (m, 3H),
7.74–7.76 (m, 2H), 7.89 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ = 20.5, 23.1, 31.1,
33.5, 46.7, 51.9, 66.4, 125.8, 126.7, 128.3, 128.4, 128.6, 131.7, 132.5,
141.8, 166.1, 178.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mannich-type reaction, solid-supported catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Polymer-Micelle Incarcerated Scandium as a Polymer-Supported Catalyst for
High-Throughput Organic Synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Takeuchi, Masahiro; Akiyama, Ryo; Kobayashi, Shu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2005), 127(38), 13096-13097

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME316 STEP1
$RXN



