$DATUM (1'S,2R,4''S,5''S)-2-[(5-Benzyloxymethyl-2,2-dimethyl-[1,3]dioxolan-4-yl)hydroxymethyl]-5-oxo-2,5-dihydropyrrole-1-carboxylic
Acid tert-Butyl Ester (13).
N-(tert-Butoxycarbonyl)-2-[(tert-butyldimethyl)siloxy]pyrrole 12 (5.0 g,
16.8 mmol) and protected L-threose 5 (4.20 g, 16.8 mmol) were dissolved
in anhydrous Et2O (50 mL) under argon and the mixture was cooled to -80
°C. At room temperature, a 1M solution of SnCl4 in CH2Cl2 (23.52 mL, 23.5
mmol) was then added via cannula over 10 min and the resulting mixture
was stirred for 5 h at -80 °C. The reaction mixture was quenched at this
temperature by adding saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution and allowed to
reach room temperature. Extraction with Et2O, drying over MgSO4, and
concentration under reduced pressure furnished a crude residue which was
purified by silica gel flash chromatography (65:35 hexanes/EtOAc) to
afford lactam 13 (5.83 g, 80%) as a white solid
(1'S,2R,4''S,5''S)-2-[(5-Benzyloxymethyl-2,2-dimethyl-[1,3]dioxolan-4-yl)hydroxymethyl]-5-oxo-2,5-dihydropyrrole-1-carboxylic
Acid tert-Butyl Ester (13), 5.83 g, 80% yield mp 96-98 °C; [α]20D +137.5
(c 0.72, CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.35 (m, 6H), 6.12 (dd, J =
6.0, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 4.77 (dt, J = 5.2, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 4.59 (s, 2H), 4.23 (d,
J = 2.4 Hz, 1H), 4.13 (ddd, J = 8.4, 5.2, 2.8 Hz, 1H), 4.06 (td, J = 7.6,
4.8 Hz, 1H), 3.76 (dd, J = 9.2, 4.4 Hz, 1H), 3.54 (t, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H),
3.52 (dd, J = 8.8, 7.2 Hz, 1H), 1.55 (s, 9H), 1.31 (s, 3H), 1.29 (s, 3H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 168.8, 150.3, 147.2, 136.6, 128.5 (2C), 128.1,
127.9 (2C), 127.6, 109.9, 83.1, 79.9, 78.8, 74.0, 72.6, 70.5, 65.7, 28.2
(3C), 26.7 (2C). Anal. Calcd for C23H31NO7: C, 63.73; H, 7.21; N, 3.23.
Found: C, 63.59; H, 7.08; N, 3.11.
