$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative experimental procedure for
Mukaiyama aldol reaction of peptides: To a suspension of the peptide
aldehyde 2a (0.078 g, 0.49 mmol) in sodium phosphate buffer, pH 7.0, (2.5
mL) was added the silyl ketene acetal (0.98 mmol) and stirred for 1 day.
The aqueous solution was then extracted with EtOAc (5 x 5 mL). The
combined organic phase was dried over MgSO4. After filtration and solvent
evaporation, the crude was purified by flash chromatography using 0-70%
ethyl actate in hexane as the eluent.
6-Amino-2-{(S)-2-[(S)-2-((S)-3-hydroxy-2-{2-[(S)-2-(2-hydroxy-3-methoxycarbonyl-3-methyl
butyryl
amino)-3-methyl-pentanoylamino]-acetylamino}-propionylamino)-4-methyl-pentanoylamino]propionyl
amino}-hexanoic aci (3c). Obtained as yellow gum (0.100 g, 80% yield). 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD) δ 0.92-0.98 (m, 17H), 1.12 (s, 3H), 1.24 (s, 4H),
1.29-1.41 (m, 6H), 1.46-1.48 (m, 2H), 1.57-1.94 (m, 13H), 2.9 (bs, 2.5H),
3.69, 3.70 (s, 3H), 3.77-3.99 (m, 6H), 4.13-4.30 (m, 6H) ppm. 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CD3OD) δ 11.5, 11.6, 16.1, 16.2, 17.3, 17.4, 19.5, 20.3, 21.7,
21.8, 23.1, 23.5, 23.7, 23.8, 23.9, 24.0, 25.9, 26.0, 26.2, 26.4, 28.0,
32.3, 38.1, 38.5, 40.8, 40.9, 41.0, 44.2, 44.5, 47.9, 48.0, 50.0, 51.4,
51.6, 52.7, 52.8, 54.3, 54.4, 54.5, 54.7, 57.9, 58.5, 59.2, 59.6, 62.5,
62.6, 76.7, 76.9, 170.5, 172.5, 173.0, 173.7, 173.9, 174.5, 174.9, 175.0,
175.3, 175.4, 175.5, 175.7, 175.9, 177.0, 177.1 ppm. LRMS (ESI) m/z
calculated for C33H60N7O12 [M+H]+ 746.42, found: 746.48. HRMS (ESI+) m/z
calculated for C33H60N7O12 [M+H]+ 746.4300, found 746.4303.
