$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Butenolide 24. 25 Copper complex 23 (2.89 g, 3.07 mmol, 0.10 equiv) was
dissolved in CH2Cl2 (38 mL), 2,2,2-trifluoroethanol (2.25 mL, 31 mmol,
1.0 equiv) was added, the solution was cooled to −77 °C (internal
temperature monitoring) with vigorous stirring. Enolsilane 21 (6.0 g, 38
mmol, 1.2 equiv) was added dropwise by cannula over 6.5 min, during which
time the brilliant blue solution changed to a deep blue-green color.
Immediately after the addition of the enolsilane was complete,
syringe-pump addition of a solution of (benzyloxy)acetaldehyde 22 (4.61
g, 30.7 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in dichloromethane (10 mL) was performed over 90
min. After 5 h at –77 °C, the cold reaction mixture was poured onto a
column of silica gel, the column was flushed with Et2O (1.4 L), and the
clear organic solution was concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
dissolved in EtOAc (0.1 L) and aq. HCl (1 M, 30 drops) and stirred for 1
h. The organic solution was diluted with EtOAc (20 mL), washed sat. aq.
NaHCO3 (10 mL), diluted with hexanes (20 mL), washed with brine (20 mL),
dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. 1H NMR
spectroscopic analysis of the unpurified reaction mixture revealed that
the reaction had run to 93% conversion and that the ratio of
diastereomers was 93:7 (C32-C33). The resultant oil was purified by flash
chromatography (80-100% Et2O in hexanes) to provide butenolide 24 (5.98
g, 97% ee) as an oil that was 95% pure by 1H NMR spectroscopic analysis
(5.7 g, 79% yield). The material was isomerically pure but was
contaminated with 5% of 2(5H)- furanone, which was not
separated.Enantiomeric excess was determined by HPLC analysis (Chiralpak
ODH, 10% i-PrOH/hexanes 0.7 mL/min, 254 nm detection, T r (minor) = 26.7
min, T r (major) = 40.3). TLC R f = 0.10 (40% EtOAc in hexanes); [α]23 D
−87 (c 4.59, CH2Cl2); IR (neat) 3444, 3091, 3031, 2910, 2868, 1748, 1600,
1455, 1361, 1164, 1091, 895, 819, 739, 698 cm−1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 7.66 (dd, 1H, J = 6, 1.5 Hz, C31H), 7.40–7.30 (m, 5H, Ph), 6.15 (dd,
1H, J = 6, 2 Hz, C30H), 5.05 (ddd, 1H, J = 7.0, 2, 1.5 Hz, C32H), 4.58
(d, 1H, J = 12 Hz, PhCHa), 4.57 (d, 1H, J = 12 Hz, PhCHb), 3.80–3.68 (m,
3H, C33H, C34H2 ), 2.88–2.76 (br s, 1H, OH); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
172.8, 155.2, 137.2, 128.5, 128.0, 127.8, 122.0, 82.8, 73.6, 71.2, 70.4;
Exact mass calcd for C13H15O4 [(M+H)+]: 235.0970; found: 235.0965 (ESI).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mukaiyama aldol reaction, 97% ee
