$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Desilylation of
Mukaiyama Aldol Compounds. To a mixture of 10 (without purification, 1.0
mmol) in MeOH (5 mL) and THF (2-5 mL) was added 12% HCl(aq) (2.1 mL, 7
mmol), and then the resulting mixture was stirred for an additional 6 h
at 30 °C. After evaporation of most of the MeOH and THF, the resulting
residue was extracted with Et2O (10 mL × 6). The organic layer was washed
with brine and dried over Na2SO4. Purification of the product by silica
gel column chromatography (n-hexane:Et2O = 3:1) afforded 12.
2-[(3-Chlorophenyl)hydroxymethyl]-3,3,3-trifluoro-2-hydroxypropanoic acid
methyl ester (12b). 79%; white powder; Diastereomeric mixture (64:36 by
1H NMR); mp 106-108 °C; IR (neat) 3508, 2965, 1754, 1760, 1600, 15780,
1480, 1442 cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz) δ 2.71 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H, minor), 3.00
(d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H, major), 3.75 (s, 3H, major), 3.98 (s, 1H, major),
3.99 (s, 3H, minor), 4.19 (s, 1H, minor), 5.17 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H,
minor), 5.23 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H, major), 7.18-7.48 (m, 4H x 2, major and
minor mixed); 19F NMR (282 MHz) δ 87.88 (s, 3F, major), 87.90 (s, 3F,
minor); EI MS m/z (relative intensity) 298 (M+, trace), 141 (100), 113
(36), 77 (69); Anal. Calcd for C11H10ClF3O4: C, 44.24; H, 3.38. Found; C,
44.04; H, 3.46.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM 64:36 diastereomeric ratio
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation and Synthetic Application of a Novel Ketene Silyl Acetal of
Methyl Trifluoropyruvate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Takikawa, Go; Katagiri, Toshimasa; Uneyama, Kenji
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2005), 70(22), 8811-8816

