$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reagents: 2-methylcyclohexanone (56 mg, 0.5 mmol),
3-methyl-2-(trimethylsilyloxy)furan 2b (128 mg, 0.75 mmol), and
Bi(OTf)3•4H2O (18 mg, 0.025 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at
-45 °C for 3 h, then at 0 °C for 1 extra h. The mixture was brought back
to room temperature and the reaction was diluted with tetrahydrofuran
(1.0 mL) and quenched with 10% aqueous HCl (1.0 mL). The biphasic sytem
was stirred for 0.25 h at room temperature, neutralized by addition of
NaHCO3 saturated solution, and extracted with ethyl acetate. The organic
phases were combined, dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated under reduced
pressure (rotary evaporator). The syn/anti ratios were determined by 1H
NMR analysis of the crude mixture:
anti(R)-5-(1R,2S)/syn(S)-5-(1R,2S)/(anti(R)-5-(1R,2R) + syn(S)-5-(1R,2R))
= 73:10:(9 + 8). The crude product was purified on silica gel (2 % ethyl
acetate/hexane) to afford 81 mg (78%) of 3n’ as a single diastereoisomer
(colorless solid). mp 80-84 °C; Rf = 0.21 (20% ethyl acetate/hexane); 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.02 (dq, J = 1.7, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 5.10 (dq, J =
1.7, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 1.95 (dd, J = 1.7, 1.7 Hz, 3H), 1.77 (br s, 1H), 1.67
(m, 1H), 1.36-1.56 (m, 7H), 1.16 (m, 1H), 1.09 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3H); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 174.9, 145.2, 131.5, 86.5, 74.7, 37.7, 31.3,
30.5, 25.7, 20.8, 15.7, 11.0; IR (KBr): 3469, 1771 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (isomer mix.)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Diastereoselective Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction of 2-(Trimethylsilyloxy)furan
Catalyzed by Bismuth Triflate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ollevier, Thierry; Bouchard, Jean-Emmanuel; Desyroy, Valerie
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2008), 73(1), 331-334

